<version>1.0.0</version>
<language>Rust</language>
Output src/su2.rs. std only. SU(2) as unit quaternions q = (a0, a1, a2, a3) <-> a0 1 + i (a1 s1 + a2 s2 + a3 s3) with Pauli matrices s_k, so (1/2) tr U = a0. Struct Quaternion { pub a: [f64;4] } with mul (matrix product order), conj (= inverse for unit quaternions), add, scale, norm_sq, half_trace (= a0), identity, normalized. Sampling with a philox::Stream: haar (uniform on S^3 via four Gaussians from Box-Muller); heat_bath(staple: Quaternion, beta, stream) returning U distributed as exp(beta * a0(U W)) dU Haar, W the staple sum: k = |W|, V = W/k, draw X with density proportional to sqrt(1-x0^2) exp(beta k x0) by the Kennedy-Pendleton algorithm (Phys. Lett. B 156 (1985) 393): repeat lambda^2 = -(ln r1 + cos^2(2 pi r2) ln r3)/(2 beta k), accept with probability sqrt(1 - lambda^2) using r4^2 <= 1 - lambda^2, x0 = 1 - 2 lambda^2; then (x1,x2,x3) uniform on the sphere of radius sqrt(1-x0^2); return X V^dagger. For beta k below 1e-12 return haar. overrelax(u, staple) returning V^dagger U^dagger V^dagger, which keeps a0(U W) fixed. A test-only flag in heat_bath_broken that skips the accept step (negative control). Independent tests: tests/su2.rs: group laws to 1e-14; haar moments E[a0^2] = 1/4, E[a0^4] = 1/8; heat-bath marginal E[a0(UW)/k] equals I_2(beta k)/I_1(beta k) for beta k in {0.5, 2, 5} within 6 standard errors; overrelax preserves the local action to 1e-13 and is an involution.
